       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.    TINVGEN.
       AUTHOR.        CR KALMAN.
       INSTALLATION.  GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER CO.
       DATE-WRITTEN.  MARCH 1992.

      *D* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
      *D*     BATCH INVOICE GENERATOR.                                *
      *D*                                                             *
      *D*     THIS PROGRAM CREATES INVOICES USING ONLY PO AND         *
      *D*     RECEIVING SLIP INFORMATION. THESE INVOICES ARE          *
      *D*     CREATED FOR THE VENDORS DESIGNATED AS "INVOICELESS".    *
      *D*     NO MANUAL ENTERING OF INVOICES IS NEEDED FOR THE        *
      *D*     PAY UPON RECEIPT CONCEPT.                               *
      *D*                                                             *
      *D*     ONE RECEIVING SLIP CREATES ONE INVOICE. THE RECEIVING   *
      *D*     SLIP ITEM IS USED TO FIND ASSOCIATED RECORDS IN         *
      *D*     SEVERAL FILES. THE INFORMATION NEEDED TO GENERATE AN    *
      *D*     INVOICE IS EDITED AND STORED IN THE INVOICE TABLE.      *
      *D*     IF THE DATA IS OK, AN INVOICE IS GENERATED FROM THE     *
      *D*     TABLE AND A SUMMARY REPORT IS PRINTED. OTHERWISE,       *
      *D*     THE TABLE IS USED TO PRINT AN ERROR REPORT.             *
      *D*                                                             *
      *D*     ABSTFILE CONCEPT...........                             *
      *D* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
      *C*
      *C*  CHANGES
      *C*  DECEMBER 17, 1992      CR KALMAN       REQ: NONE
      *C*  AFTER PROCESSING AN ABSTFILE THAT CONTAINED NO RECEIVERS
      *C*  THE PROGRAM BLEW UP WHEN TRYING TO PROCESS THE NEXT ABSTFILE.
      *C*  FIXED THE PROGRAM TO PROPERLY CLOSE THE TEMPORARY FILES IN
      *C*  THE LOGIC IT FOLLOWS WHEN THERE ARE NO RECEIVERS.
      *C*
      *C*  JANUARY   4, 1993      CR KALMAN       REQ: NONE
      *C*  ADDED CODE TO PRINT THE RAW MATERIAL REPORT HDGS WITH A
      *C*  SHORT MSG STATING THAT NONE OF THE INVOICES GENERATED
      *C*  WERE FOR RAW MATERIALS. THIS REPORT WAS PREVIOUSLY BEING
      *C*  SKIPPED WHEN THIS SITUATION OCCURED.
      *C*
      *C*  JANUARY   4, 1993      CR KALMAN       REQ: NONE
      *C*  PACKING SLIP FIELD ON ERROR REPORT WAS NOT CORRECTLY BEING
      *C*  CLEARED OUT FOR THE NEXT ERROR BEING PRINTED. FIXED THIS.
      *C*
      *C*  JANUARY  11, 1993      CR KALMAN       REQ: 6375
      *C*  IT WAS REALIZED THAT GENERATED INVOICES COULD POSSIBLY
      *C*  CONTAIN THE SAME INVOICE NUMBER FOR THE SAME VENDOR.  THIS
      *C*  WOULD OCCUR IN CASES OF MATERIAL RECEIPTS THAT WERE FOR
      *C*  MORE THAN 12 ITEMS FOR THE SAME PO NUMBER (ALL WOULD USE
      *C*  THE SAME PACKING SLIP).  IT WOULD ALSO OCCUR IN CASES OF
      *C*  "REFER BACK" WHERE MULTIPLE PO'S WOULD COME FROM ONE VENDOR
      *C*  IN THE SAME SHIPMENT USING THE SAME PACKING SLIP.  IT WAS
      *C*  DECIDED THAT THE CURRENT ADDED PREFIX OF "PK" WOULD BE
      *C*  CHANGEABLE. IN OTHER WORDS, THE FIRST GENERATED INVOICE
      *C*  WOULD CONTAIN "PK", THE SECOND WOULD BE "PA", THIRD "PB"
      *C*  AND SO ON UP TO "PZ". AFTER "PZ" AN ERROR MESSAGE WILL
      *C*  APPEAR ON THE ERROR REPORT AND THE USER WILL HAVE TO
      *C*  HANDLE MANUALLY.
      *C*
      *C*  FEBRUARY 23, 1992      CR KALMAN       REQ: 6376
      *C*  ADDED "ACCOUNTS PAYABLE" TO REPORT HEADINGS TO MAKE THEM
      *C*  EASIER TO FIND ON SHARED PRINTERS. (UNC WAS HAVING A PROBLEM.)
      *C*
      *C*  MARCH 3, 1993          CR KALMAN       REQ: 6377
      *C*  ADDED TERMS TO INVOICE GENERATION SUMMARY REPORT BY
      *C*  REQUEST OF BONNIE NAPIER IN UNCITY.
      *C*
      *C*  MARCH 22, 1993         CR KALMAN       REQ: 6387
      *C*  ADDED TOTALS LINE TO SUMMARY REPORT SHOWING TOTAL NET DUE
      *C*  VENDOR AND TOTAL NUMBER OF REGISTERS.
      *C*
      *C*  JUNE 17, 1993          CR KALMAN
      *C*  PUT TAX CODE OF FIRST ITEM INTO DINVRCD TAX CODE INSTEAD
      *C*  OF BLANKS.  IT WAS SHOWING UP ON THE INVOICE MONTH END
      *C*  SUMMARY REPORT AS A BLANK TAX CODE.
      *C*
      *C*  OCTOBER 20, 1993       CR KALMAN
      *C*  1. ADDED THE VENDOR NAME TO THE ERROR REPORT FOR EASIER
      *C*     VISIBILITY BY THE USER.
      *C*  2. WILL NOW ALLOW INVOICES TO BE PAID EVEN THO AN ITEM
      *C*     MAY HAVE A ZERO QUANTITY.
      *C*
      *C*  MARCH 24, 1994         CR KALMAN       REQ: 6489
      *C*  FOUND A WAY THAT AN INVOICE WITH QTY RECEIVED = 0 FOR
      *C*  ALL ITEMS COULD SNEAK THRU AND GET PAID. IT WOULD OCCUR ON
      *C*  A ONE ITEM INVOICE WHEN THERE WAS MORE THAN ONE RCV'G CORRECTION
      *C*  TC FOR THAT DAY AND THE NET OF THE TC'S WOULD EQUAL 0. THE
      *C*  TOTAL ITEM COUNT FOR THAT INVOICE WOULD ONLY REFLECT ONE
      *C*  OF THE TC'S (IE, A NON-ZERO NUMBER) WHILE THE INDIVIDUAL
      *C*  ITEM COUNT WOULD REFLECT ALL THE TC'S (IE, A ZERO NUMBER).
      *C*
      *C*  MAY 02, 1994           CR KALMAN
      *C*  CHANGED CODE SO THAT ACCRUED TAX WOULD BE LOWERED BY THE
      *C*  THE DISCOUNT AMOUNT IF THE PLANT HAS THEIR FLAG SET TO
      *C*  TAKE ADVANTAGE OF THIS.
      *C*
      *C*  MAY 19, 1994           CR KALMAN        REQ: 6506
      *C*  ADDED CODE TO MAKE THE MESSAGE "**OVER**" APPEAR ON THE
      *C*  INVOICE GEN SUM RPT IF THE INVOICE (NON RAW MATL ONLY)
      *C*  GOES OVER THE LIMIT SET BY THE PLANT IN "PODL".
      *C*
      *C   JUNE 23, 1994          CR KALMAN
      *C   ADDED CALL TO COBOL ERROR HANDLER -MCXCBLERR.
      *C*
      *C*  OCTOBER 26, 1994       CA ZUBEK
      *C*  CHANGED THE LOGIC FOR PLACING THE VENDOR NAME ON THE
      *C*  SUMMARY REPORT (GENSUMFL).  INSTEAD OF BLOWING UP WHEN
      *C*  A VENDOR NAME IS NOT FOUND IN DVENDOR, AN ERROR MESSAGE
      *C*  WILL BE PRINTED SHOWING THE VENDOR CODE IN ERROR.
      *C*  (UNION CITY HAD A PROBLEM WITH THIS SITUATION.)
      *C*
      *C*  APRIL 20, 1995         CA ZUBEK
      *C*  CHANGED HOW 323 AND 423 TRANSACTIONS ARE HANDLED.  BEFORE,
      *C*  THE QUANTITY IN DRCVITEM WAS USED TO GENERATE THE INVOICE
      *C*  AMOUNT FOR TC 323 AND 423.  ANY CORRECTIONS AFTERWARD WERE NOT
      *C*  CONSIDERED.  HOWEVER, THIS CREATED A PROBLEM WHEN A PLANT IS
      *C*  USING THE DELAY FACTOR FOR INVOICELESS PROCESSING.  IF ANY
      *C*  CORRECTIONS HAVE OCCURRED BEFORE THE DELAY, AN INACCURATE
      *C*  QUANTITY IS USED BECAUSE IT DOESN'T CONSIDER ANY CHANGES
      *C*  FROM THE SAME DAY AS THE 323. INSTEAD OF TAKING THE AMOUNT
      *C*  FROM DRCVITEM, THE LOGIC WAS CHANGED TO JUST USE THE
      *C*  TRANSACTION INFORMATION IN THE ABSTFILE.
      *C*
      *C*  APRIL 27, 1995          CA ZUBEK
      *C*  HAD TO CORRECT A PROBLEM REVEALED BY THE LAST CORRECTION MADE
      *C*  TO THIS PROGRAM.  THE DRCVITEM QTY WAS NO LONGER BEING USED TO
      *C*  FIGURE OUT THE INVOICE QTY (EXPLAINED IN THE LAST COMMENT), BUT
      *C*  THE UNIT OF MEASURE FROM DRCVITEM WAS STILL BEING USED.
      *C*  HOWEVER, THE RECEIVED UM IS NOT ALWAYS THE SAME AS THE
      *C*  DPOITEM UM, SO THE PROGRAM WAS CHANGED TO USE THE ABSTFILE UM.
      *C*  SEVERAL NEW FIELDS WERE ADDED TO ALLOW FOR THIS CHANGE.
      *C*
      *C*  JUNE 5, 1995            CA YODER
      *C*  ADDED DISPLAY STATEMENT TO SHOW WHICH ABSTFILE THE PROGRAM IS
      *C*  USING.  ALSO ADDED PO NUMBER TO BLOW-UP MESSAGE TO HELP IN
      *C*  PROBLEM-SOLVING.
      *C*
      *C*  JUNE 14, 1995           CA YODER
      *C*  CHANGED 9999-CONVERT-QTY TO SET A SWITCH IN THE ERROR TABLE
      *C*  TO INDICATE WHEN THE READ OF MSTORERM FAILED INSTEAD OF BLOWING
      *C*  UP.
      *C*
      *C*  JUNE 15, 1995           CA YODER
      *C*  ADDED THE ABILITY TO RECOGNIZE BATCH RECEIVING TRANSACTIONS
      *C*  523, 524, 623, AND 624.  WHEN THE PROGRAM READS ONE OF THESE
      *C*  TRANSACTIONS, IT WILL CONVERT THE TC NUMBER TO ITS RESPECTIVE
      *C*  3XX TRANSACTION AND PROCESS AS USUAL.
      *C*
      *C*  JUNE 16, 1995           CA YODER
      *C*  ADDED LOGIC TO HANDLE 923 TRANSACTIONS, WHICH GIVE THE DECIMAL
      *C*  VALUE FOR THE QUANTITY INSTEAD OF THE ROUNDED VALUE.  THE 923
      *C*  TRANSACTIONS ARE LOADED INTO A TABLE AND READ AS NEEDED WHEN
      *C*  PROCESSING THE INVOICES.  THE DECIMAL QUANTITY IS USED INSTEAD
      *C*  OF THE ROUNDED QUANTITY IN THE ABSTFILES SO THAT THE CORRECT
      *C*  INVOICE AMOUNT IS PAID.
      *C*
      *C*  JULY 28, 1995           CA YODER
      *C*  ADDED LOGIC TO PRINT AN ERROR MESSAGE WHEN A VENDOR IS NOT
      *C*  INVOICELESS.  THE ACCOUNTS PAYABLE DEPTS. HAVE TROUBLE FINDING
      *C*  THE PROBLEM WHEN AN INVOICE ISN'T PAID DUE TO THE VENDOR NOT
      *C*  BEING INVOICELESS--ESPECIALLY IF THE STATUS HAS BEEN CHANGED.
      *C*  THIS MESSAGE SHOULD HELP ALERT THEM TO THE PROBLEM.
      *C*
      *C*  DECEMBER 20, 1995       CA YODER
      *C*  ADDED LOGIC TO START REGISTER NUMBERS OVER IF 99999 IS
      *C*  REACHED.  LAWTON CALLED AND SAID THEY HAD A PROBLEM WITH
      *C*  REGISTER NUMBERS STARTING OVER A FEW YEARS AGO AND ASKED IF
      *C*  ANYTHING COULD BE DONE.
      *C*
      *C*  FEBRUARY 9, 1996        CA YODER
      *C*  CORRECTED PROBLEM WHERE AN INVOICE OF 0 QTY WOULD BE WRITTEN
      *C*  TO THE DATABASES.  THE CAUSE OF THE PROBLEM WAS WHEN SEVERAL
      *C*  ITEMS WERE RECEIVED FOR THE SAME PO AND ONE OF THE ITEMS
      *C*  WAS CORRECTED TO 0 QTY.  SO, THERE WERE VALID INVOICE
      *C*  TRANSACTIONS FOR THE PO, BUT THE 0 QTY INVOICE WAS STILL
      *C*  CARRIED THROUGH THE PROGRAM WITH THE OTHER INVOICES.  A
      *C*  CHECK WAS ADDED TO 9-6-MAIN TO SKIP WRITING INVOICES WITH
      *C*  A QUANTITY OF 0.
      *C*
      *C*  JULY 15, 1996           CA YODER
      *C*  MODIFIED FOR CENTURY DATABASE CHANGES.
      *C*
      *C*  MAY 13, 1997            CA YODER
      *C*  ADDED PO NUMBER TO BLOWUP MESSAGE FOR INVALID TAX CODE.
      *C*
      *C*  DEC 08, 1997            CA YODER
      *C*  ADDED THE CENTURY DATE TO THE HEADER FOR THE GENSUMFL
      *C*  REPORT.  Y2K TESTING FOUND THAT THE TINVRPT SCREEN DID NOT
      *C*  INCLUDE CENTURY IN THE DATE SORT LOGICAL FILE.  THE SECOND
      *C*  DATE WILL BE THE PRIMARY SORT FIELD, AND THE FIRST DATE WILL
      *C*  BE THE SECONDARY SORT FIELD.
      *C*
      *C*  JAN 30, 1998            CA YODER
      *C*  RECEIVING WAS CHANGED TO REMOVE THE RESTRICTION OF 12 ITEMS
      *C*  PER RECEIVING SLIP.  INCREASED THE TABLE SIZE IN THIS PROGRAM
      *C*  TO HANDLE UP TO 1000 ITEMS.
      *C*
      *C*  06/07/99   CA YODER   (DECATUR REQUEST)
      *C*  RE-COMPILED TO PICK UP MTAX DATABASE CHANGE TO
      *C*  EXPAND TAX RATE PERCENTAGE FROM 2 DECIMAL PLACES TO 4.
      *C*
      *C*  APR 20, 2000            CA YODER      (DANVILLE REQUEST)
      *C*  ADDED LITERAL TO SHOW WHEN AN INVOICE IS GENERATED WITH A
      *C*  DEPARTMENT OF "0000".
      *C*
      *C*  CREATED ANOTHER OUTPUT FILE TO SHOW ALL OF THE NO-CHECK
      *C*  INVOICES THAT WERE GENERATED.
      *C*
      *C*  FEB 25, 2003            CA YODER      (DANVILLE REQUEST)
      *C*  ADDED LOGIC TO SHOW "**OVER**" LITERAL WHEN A RAW MATERIAL
      *C*  INVOICE ITEM HAS A CLASS IN THE 200 OR 300 RANGE AND IS
      *C*  OVER THE NON-RAW MATERIAL DOLLAR LIMIT.
      *C*

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.

